== trace steers to the descriptor, stdout still shows:
hi
== captured at the descriptor:
+ echo hi
+ set +x
== an external child inherits the numbered descriptor:
external
== without BASH_XTRACEFD the trace stays on stderr:
+ echo hi
+ set +x
== an unparsable BASH_XTRACEFD falls back to stderr:
+ echo hi
+ set +x
== assignments, arrays, loops, and redirections trace by syntax owner:
+ scalar=value
+ scalar+=tail
+ arr=(one 'two three')
+ empty=()
+ arr+=(four)
+ PFX=value
+ printf '%s\n' ok
ok
+ for i in a b
+ : a
+ for i in a b
+ : b
+ printf done
+ set +x
